      "blocks": {
        "heading_iq8pi8": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Is DTF Transfer? A Complete Beginner’s Guide",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_8UaPVj": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>If you're new to custom apparel printing, you've probably heard the term <strong>DTF transfer</strong>. But what exactly is DTF, how does it work, and why has it become such a popular option for T-shirts, hoodies, workwear, tote bags, and custom merchandise?</p><p>DTF stands for <strong>Direct to Film</strong>. Instead of printing directly onto a garment, the design is first printed onto a special transfer film. The finished transfer is then applied to the garment using heat and pressure.</p><p>For creators, apparel brands, print shops, and small businesses, DTF offers a flexible way to produce vibrant, detailed designs without the setup required by many traditional printing methods.</p><p>In this beginner's guide, we'll explain how DTF printing works, where it can be used, its biggest advantages, and how to get started.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_iq8pi8",
        "text_8UaPVj"
