    "multicolumn_tFC3De": {
      "type": "multicolumn",
      "blocks": {
        "column_686kDL": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "1. Prepare the Artwork",
            "text": "<p>The process begins with a digital design.</p><p>High-quality artwork helps preserve small details, clean edges, gradients, and text during printing. Transparent-background artwork is particularly useful when the final design should not have a visible rectangular background.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_YM9eAh": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "2. Print the Design Onto DTF Film",
            "text": "<p>The artwork is printed onto coated PET transfer film using specialized DTF inks.</p><p>Color inks create the artwork, while a white ink underbase helps maintain opacity and color vibrancy, especially when the transfer is applied to dark garments.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_fhhyRz": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "3. Apply Adhesive Powder",
            "text": "<p>While the printed ink is prepared for production, hot-melt adhesive powder is applied to the printed area.</p><p>This powder ultimately creates the bonding layer between the printed design and the fabric.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_U7VEer": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "4. Cure the Transfer",
            "text": "<p>The film is heated under controlled conditions to cure the adhesive.</p><p>After curing, the transfer becomes a ready-to-press product that can be stored, shipped, and applied later.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_RJLVRk": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "5. Heat Press the Transfer",
            "text": "<p>The transfer is positioned on the garment and applied using the appropriate combination of:</p><p><strong>Temperature + Time + Pressure</strong></p><p>Exact settings can vary depending on the transfer system and fabric, so always follow the application instructions supplied with your transfers.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_LMbqcN": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "6. Peel and Finish",
            "text": "<p>After the initial press, the carrier film is peeled according to the recommended hot-, warm-, or cold-peel instructions.</p><p>Some transfer systems also recommend a finishing press.</p><p>That's it—the original digital artwork is now applied to the garment.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
